          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP777 - FTR Hinton

Posted: N 53° 22.080 W 117° 37.952

My GPSr: N 53° 22.078 W 117° 37.948

(FOUND)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was my first stop on a day-long capping run from Hinton north to Grande Cache. I'm not sure what &quot;FTR&quot; stands for exactly, but I have to think that it could have to do with the cute little &quot;Charlie Brown Christmas&quot; tree that stands guard over the cap. I know it's a stretch, but there has to be some connection, right? &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I parked at the convenient approach not far from the cap and walked over for a quick find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
